Algorithmic basis
-----------------
The polycistronic tRNA-gRNA (PTG) design procedure, including the engineered
gRNA scaffold offered as the default in this tool, implements and extends the
approach described in:

  Dutta, T.K., Ray, S., Akhil, V.S., Rupinikrishna, K., Chauhan, U., Dutta, A.,
  Vijayan, J., Iquebal, M.A., Chinnusamy, V. A synthetic guide RNA scaffold
  enhanced CRISPR/Cas9 editing efficiency in plants across multiple gene targets.
  International Journal of Biological Macromolecules 365, 152456 (2026).
  https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijbiomac.2026.152456

Version 2.0 extends that work with support for up to 12 spacers, 12 Type IIS
restriction enzymes, selectable native (76 nt) and engineered (86 nt) gRNA
scaffolds, configurable Cas9 plasmid vector overhangs, and internal recognition
site detection.


